mode: "100644"
text: "# Building the moment calendar + two worked examples\n\n## The two gates (run every candidate moment through both)\n```\nFIT GATE:   Does it match our brand / audience / goals? Would our audience expect/welcome us here?\n            Can we add something beyond \"happy [day]\"? -> if no, SIT OUT.\nAUTHENTICITY GATE (identity/cause moments): Do we have genuine YEAR-ROUND commitment + a real stake?\n            \"Why us, why this moment?\" -> if no real answer, STAY QUIET (silence > performative noise).\n```\n\n## Tier table (match effort + tone to the moment)\n| Tier | Examples | Approach |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 — commercial / fun | BFCM, Halloween, Valentine's, Mother's Day, fitting food/internet days | go; promo OK; multi-week series for the big ones |\n| 2 — authentic-alignment | Pride, Earth Day, awareness months | only with real year-round commitment; substance, not a logo swap |\n| 3 — cultural / solemn | MLK Day, Juneteenth, Ramadan/Holi, remembrance days | non-promotional respect; never a sales hook; or sit out |\n\n## Lead-time table (verify-quarterly)\n```\nMAJOR (BFCM, Christmas, Valentine's, big launches): 8-12 weeks  | brief creative early; multi-week series; paid for BFCM\nMINOR (awareness/social/fun days):                  2-4 weeks   | lighter touch, single or few posts\nSeasonal milestones: brief Back-to-School in May; lock Halloween briefs in Aug / creative by early Oct\nRun on quarterly (13-week) cycles; review planned-vs-actual each quarter -> next brief\n```\n\n## Per-moment plan (one row per chosen moment)\n```\nMOMENT | DATE (2026, market) | CATEGORY | TIER | FIT? why-us | ANGLE | FORMAT(S) | CHANNEL(S) | LEAD TIME | GOAL | measure\n```\n\n## WoopSocial flow\n```\nagent maps moments + gates fit/authenticity + tiers + plans angle/lead-time\n-> big commercial moment? -> campaign-and-launch-planning (+ paid)   |   cultural-moment craft -> meme-and-culture\n-> visual -> image tools / design-and-templates\n-> feed the content-calendar -> WoopSocial SCHEDULES the planned content AHEAD. Leave ~50% open for trend-jacking.\nWoopSocial does NOT pick moments, judge authenticity, build the calendar, or run paid.\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 - e-commerce brand, Q4 (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nI'm not posting every food day. My calendar: Halloween (Tier 1, light), BFCM (Tier 1, the big one), Christmas (Tier 1, series).\nBFCM is a 3-week campaign -> campaign-and-launch-planning, briefed in September, with paid. I draft the series now, schedule it\nahead in WoopSocial, and keep ~half the calendar open for whatever trends in November. Pride? We don't do year-round work there, so we don't post -- I'm not rainbow-washing for reach.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 - wellness studio (warm studio voice)\n```\nWe pick a small handful that fit -- World Mental Health Day (we genuinely do this work year-round, so we have something real to\nsay), the seasonal shift into cozy autumn, and our own studio anniversary. Each gets a thoughtful angle, not a \"happy day\"\ngraphic. We plan them 4-8 weeks out, build the visuals in our template, and schedule them ahead -- leaving room to respond to the moment. The days we have no real reason to join, we let pass.\n```\n\nBoth: the few that fit (not every holiday); the authenticity gate honored; tiered + planned ahead; big moments as campaigns;\nscheduled in advance with room left for reactive; performative participation refused; measured against a real goal.\n"
